    "note": [
        {
            "structuredValue": [],
            "parallelValue": [],
            "groupedValue": [],
            "value": "One of the most spectacular locations of thrombolites exhibiting large macrostructures such as bowls, broccoli-shaped structures, domes, eroded-top domes, columns, overhanging domes, and pancake-shaped structures, can be seen at Lago Sarmiento, Patagonia, Chile. Microfacies and growth processes were characterized for samples taken from Lago Sarmiento to study the relationship between macro- and micro-morphologies.",
